  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5701.13 Non-conviction data",
  "priorExpiration": "2017-02-14",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5701.13 “Non-conviction data” means information indicating:\n\n(a) An arrest without disposition if one year has elapsed from the date of arrest and no active prosecution of the charge is pending;\n\n(b) That the law enforcement agency has elected not to refer a matter to a prosecutor;\n\n(c) That a prosecutor has elected not to commence criminal proceedings;\n\n(d) That proceedings have been indefinitely postponed; or\n\n(e) An acquittal or dismissal.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5700) #6704, eff 3-3-98, EXPIRED: 3-3-06\n\nNew. #8591, INTERIM, eff 3-24-06, EXPIRES: 9-20-06; ss by #8651, eff 6-2-06, EXPIRED: 6-2-14\n\nNew. #11157, INTERIM, eff 8-18-16, EXPIRED: 2-14-17\n\nNew. #12132, eff 3-17-17 (from Saf-C 5701.12)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5700.html"
}
